WEBVTT

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.950
What a horrible sound...

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:12.690
We heard that noise at Sasu yesterday...

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:14.570
"Explosives"? Is that what they're called?

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:15.700
"Explosives"...

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.550
Hey, Princess.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:23.460
Focus.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.900
We've got our own work to do.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.130
I know that.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.170
Keep them away from the archers,
no matter the cost!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.810
If any of them fall off the cliff, 
make sure they're dead!

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.020
Right!

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:49.650
Hey, look!

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.020
Shit!

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:02.700
Not bad, for an adopted son.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:07.510
You're starting to look like a general,
if I see you from just the right angle.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:11.430
You were just blind before.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.210
The enemy's hanging in there.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:54.600
There doesn't seem to be 
many of them, though...

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.740
Want to use the Shintenrai 
on them again, and see if that works?

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.260
If I may, Uriyan Edei-san,

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:05.470
we don't need to waste 
valuable Shintenrai here.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:07.870
Another charge will end this.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.590
The Shintenrai and our brethren...

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.040
Which of the two is more important?

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:15.360
I-I'll get to it immediately!

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:21.350
The older a man gets,

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:24.270
the more he starts to try and calculate 
the value of lives with money...

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.590
Uriyan Edei-san.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.220
The Shintenrai will work nicely,

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.470
but I do have a suggestion...

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.480
<b>Soldier in Uriyan Edei's Army: 
Karaun</b>

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.810
What is it, Karaun?

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.120
So that's the Mongol general?

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:39.240
We take down the two of them and run.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.190
If you were good enough to take out 
those scouts, you can do it here.

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:44.600
Or maybe that was just luck...

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:48.070
Want me to aim for 
that bullseye on your hat?

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:51.410
<i>Calm down...</i>

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:55.000
<i>If we can kill that general, 
it will delay them a lot.</i>

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:55.960
Let's do it.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.170
<i>Calm down, my heart..</i>

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:03.280
<i>I need to make up for my failure before...</i>

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:07.960
<i>When I let my rage take over, 
and put everyone in danger...</i>

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:10.260
<i>Don't look at the target.</i>

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:14.390
<i>Look at the path the arrow must travel, 
and imagine carrying it along that path...</i>

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:15.750
<i>And fire!</i>

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:17.470
<i>Got him!</i>

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:24.770
I'm lucky to have a man like you.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.950
We failed.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:31.200
It doesn't matter. This was 
just a way to kill some time.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:32.360
Let's get out of here.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:35.540
Princess, hurry!

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:44.260
She's beautiful...

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.790
Wow! We can't kill her.

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:52.440
Hey, is there some way 
we can capture her unharmed?

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:56.020
She would be the best 
war prize we could get.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.600
Yes. Leave it to me.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:03.950
We took out the ones on the inside.

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:08.650
Everybody's exhausted, but it seems 
the Mongols have calmed down.

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:13.360
No... Another force 
is heading into the valley.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:16.810
They're going along the river 
to strike us from behind.

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.490
General, it's time to bail.

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:20.780
Okay.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:23.800
Everyone, we're leaving!

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.830
You all fought well!

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:28.020
Yes, sir!

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:32.330
I always knew he was 
a talented archer, but...

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:34.380
Yeah. He seems totally different now.

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:38.050
If our lord was here, 
he would be quite pleased.

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:41.950
Good work, rookie.

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:47.040
I can't let an exile take all the glory.

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:50.490
More explosives...

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:51.790
We're done here.

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:54.420
Get the men out of here.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:59.120
I'll hit them when they 
peer out from behind their shields.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:04.390
<i>What's that tube?</i>

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:27.740
Y-Yajirou-dono!

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:29.280
I see.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.190
So that's a "gun."

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:35.110
Yes. We put gunpowder in a tube 
and use it to fire a bullet.

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:37.230
I've heard rumors of it.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:40.530
It was used against the barbarian 
tribes of Europe, I'm told.

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:42.620
Well, it's almost impossible to aim,

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:44.160
and a hassle to use.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:46.750
Used on its own, it's simply a toy,

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:49.430
but the Chinese seemed eager to try it.

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:53.020
Don't let them have too much fun.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:54.720
It hit!

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:58.110
Great job. Remember how that felt—

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:11.070
They're retreating!

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:14.880
Yajirou-dono! Yajirou-dono!

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:24.620
Yajirou...

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.690
<i>Don't laugh, Jinzaburou.</i>

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:43.940
<i>But to tell you the truth...</i>

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.380
<i>I'm still not sure.</i>

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:55.690
<i>What is the point of this battle?</i>

00:07:56.980 --> 00:08:00.350
<i>What will happen to Tsushima?</i>

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:07.340
<i>Where does my death lead?</i>

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:13.250
<i>Only you can decide what your war is.</i>

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.100
<i>But...</i>

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:18.800
Yajirou!

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:23.110
I won't let your death...

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:25.590
...go to waste...

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:42.760
His life was just beginning...

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:57.390
Princess.

00:08:58.090 --> 00:09:00.850
Everyone, I'm glad you're safe.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.970
I heard a noise like thunder.

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:07.260
Oh, did you kill the general?

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.280
I failed.

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:16.780
I see. We lost our own general.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.900
Abiru Yajirou-dono.

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:25.040
Take him.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:27.910
He was a brave warrior.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:33.100
I see...

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:41.510
I shall see to his burial soon.

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:49.510
Unlike my father and brother...

00:09:49.510 --> 00:09:52.000
He's still warm!

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:02.590
There are pools of blood everywhere!

00:10:02.590 --> 00:10:03.650
It's so wet!

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:05.130
What do you want, kid?

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:08.290
Oh, you guys are pissed off, huh?

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:10.380
I was keeping watch 
because you guys asked me to.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:15.370
Hey, Kuchii! The Mongols from Sasu are here.

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:17.350
The Mongols from Sasu?

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:18.370
Troops from Goryeo?

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:19.440
Yep.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:23.060
They came from the west, 
and they're almost on top of us.

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:33.060
First, they're after us from 
the east, and now the west?

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:35.240
We're pinned down.

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:40.400
We're just little fish swimming 
around in a pot called Tsushima.

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:42.960
No matter where we run, 
we'll be cooked and eaten in the end.

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:46.670
No, this may be a gift from heaven.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:50.650
What do you mean, Jinzaburou?

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:55.000
Two different groups of Mongols 
are chasing us as we flee north.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.630
<b>Sasu</b>

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.630
<b>Capital</b>

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.630
What happens if they run into each other?

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:00.290
We now have twice as many 
people after us, that's all!

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:03.640
No, the Mongols we saw at the capital

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:06.260
are totally different than 
the ones we saw at Sasu.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:09.470
Their hair, their smell, their clothes.

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:11.550
The way they fought. Everything.

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:15.990
There's more than one army 
in the Mongol ranks.

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:19.440
Which means that each army 
will have its own commander.

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:23.490
<b>Sasu</b>

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:23.490
<b>Capital</b>

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:23.480
If the two of them run into each other 
on these narrow mountain paths,

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:25.310
any confusion that occurs 
will slow them down.

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:27.700
It's almost sunset.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.860
If we can escape 
into the mountains at night,

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:31.920
we'll have the advantage 
since we know these paths.

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:36.920
We can use that confusion 
to survive the night.

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:41.670
We can live to see tomorrow...

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:46.640
If we can do that, the time that 
everyone paid for with their lives

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:47.860
will be worth something.

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:53.120
Okay!

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:55.350
Everyone, let's escape to the north!

00:11:55.350 --> 00:11:56.360
Yes, ma'am!

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:00.970
<i>Little fish in a pot...</i>

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:01.700
<i>Interesting.</i>

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:05.670
<i>Even a little fish can thrash around 
enough to overturn the pot,</i>

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:09.570
<i>and maybe, just maybe, put out the fire.</i>

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:16.750
They fled!

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:18.030
After them!

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:28.820
Hey, guys.

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:30.310
Gettin' the hell out of here, huh?

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:31.900
Onitakemaru...

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:33.350
There you are!

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:35.220
You useless moron.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:37.820
Shut up, you little monkey!

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:41.020
H-Hey, help me!

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:42.830
It's the old geezer.

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:45.100
What are you doing here?

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:46.890
Stop it, you stupid kid!

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:54.100
He threatened me and the fleeing 
farmers, then took our stuff!

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:57.950
You threatened the farmers?

00:12:57.950 --> 00:12:58.870
Is that true?

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:01.920
Onitakemaru, what are you thinking?

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:05.190
An opportunity for plunder

00:13:05.190 --> 00:13:11.090
is the best thing you can offer 
your men after a long sea journey.

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:12.330
What?

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:16.850
And the plunder only looks 
more valuable if it has a guard, right?

00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:21.120
Hurry! Many of them are wounded!

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:22.700
We can catch them!

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:28.810
There you are.

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:30.880
Hey, thieves!

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:32.570
Look over here!

00:13:32.570 --> 00:13:34.780
Look at all this treasure I've got!

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:37.800
Take it if you can!

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:40.160
Hey, untie me!

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:45.300
Now come!

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:57.440
These Mongols are pretty tough.

00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:00.080
Don't waste too much time, Onitakemaru.

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:03.560
If you stay there too long, 
you'll get surrounded from both sides.

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:05.030
Huh?

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:11.710
Oh, fine.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:23.700
See ya, treasure!

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:30.850
The treasures of the Japanese?

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:32.520
Take them.

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:34.160
Yes, sir, Chouben-sama.

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:38.380
I like this one...

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:42.380
We won this plunder for our own.

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:44.000
Don't touch it with your filthy hands.

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:47.040
I-I picked it up first!

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.620
The winner takes all.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:52.660
That's all there is to it.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:54.110
What?

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:07.730
I'm sorry I wasn't a better general!

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.550
Reporting.

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:13.560
Our vanguard is brawling
with the Goryeo forces

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:16.150
over the items left behind 
by the fleeing Japanese.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:17.860
Goryeo.

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:20.100
They must've come from the West.

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:21.190
Hey.

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:24.700
Don't let them have a single coin!

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:28.480
Yes, General!

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:17.770
<i>A samurai should be 
more elegant when he sleeps...</i>

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:34.740
Then think of my face instead,
and remember me in your heart as your father.

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:38.040
I was satisfied with the fact 
that I'd fought in the past

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:40.770
and forgot that there was 
more fighting to do.

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:44.950
Where do we run once the Mukuri come?

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:49.610
Tae... Sasamaru... I just wanted...

00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:52.650
I won't lose anyone else!

00:16:56.020 --> 00:17:00.740
Father, I'll do the best 
I can to protect it!

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:10.800
What?

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.920
Just seeing if you were still breathing.

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:21.680
As you can see, I'm fine.

00:17:22.170 --> 00:17:23.430
Good.

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:27.350
I need you to keep fighting for me.

00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:38.800
<i>So that's it.</i>

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:48.000
<i>I wondered why, even here, I was so eager 
to get involved in other people's wars.</i>

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:50.320
<i>But it's simple.</i>

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:52.450
<i>This is my war.</i>

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:57.640
<i>I'd lost everything, and finally 
had no more burdens to carry...</i>

00:17:57.640 --> 00:18:01.470
<i>But now I've been given another burden 
to carry, and I can't let it go.</i>

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:10.100
<i>Is this going to be the story of my life?</i>

00:18:27.510 --> 00:18:28.950
<i>Akimado fireflies...</i>

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:42.860
<i>Perhaps the souls of everyone 
who died were reborn as fireflies...</i>

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:53.080
<i>We failed to become fireflies.</i>

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:55.240
<i>What do we do now?</i>

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:03.700
Who's there?

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:06.200
Princess Teruhi.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:08.950
Have you forgotten me?

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:16.720
Is a man named Kuchii Jinzaburou here?

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:17.930
Jinzaburou?

00:19:18.490 --> 00:19:20.380
You lookin' for me, old man?

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:22.530
Who are you?

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:24.010
You need something from me?

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:27.860
I'll be the one to decide that.

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:33.440
Well, you seem strong.

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:36.350
But I don't like the look on your face.

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:38.050
It's vulgar.

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:40.440
Nagamine was right.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:41.800
Nagamine?

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:43.690
From the Toibarai?

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:47.130
You work for him, old man?

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:48.240
Fool.

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:50.900
You think I'd work for someone so young?

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:54.670
Follow me.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:56.870
I'll take you to the palace.

00:19:57.990 --> 00:19:59.380
"Palace"?

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:02.690
Know that a prisoner 
and exile such as yourself

00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:08.380
is unworthy to receive even 
a chance to speak with the emperor.

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:12.470
Wait.

00:20:12.470 --> 00:20:13.800
What do you mean, "emperor"?

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:20.050
<i>Emperor...</i>

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:32.610
<i>That old man's a damn fast runner...</i>

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:45.030
<i>That mountain?</i>

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:56.290
"Tohokamiemitame..."

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:01.010
<i>Damn! I lost him!</i>

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:20.250
Welcome.

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:31.410
This place, the peak of Mt. Shiratake,

00:21:31.410 --> 00:21:32.390
is the palace.

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:33.700
Old man...

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:35.720
What are you planning?

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:42.560
The emperor is here.

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:43.780
Bow.

00:21:51.220 --> 00:21:55.430
How many years has it been since 
I've seen a warrior from the east?

00:21:55.430 --> 00:21:57.950
Welcome.

00:21:57.950 --> 00:22:00.220
I am Tokihito.

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:05.240
In our capital, I am 
known as Emperor Antoku.

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:09.970
<b>Episode 6:
Where Death Leads</b>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:11.970
<b></b>
